                                  8.04.96

Small description:
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
This a small util I use to schedule my events to run, such as
polling other systems, making backups and generating stats.

It's a CyberCron clone, without locale support, and some other
small things left out, to make it as small as possible, after
all it runs on your amiga all the time in the background.

This version has no special features added, it's just a fresh
recompile and does its work ok for me.



cRon Syntax:
~~~~~~~~~~~~
These are the arguments cRon understands:

The name of the cRonTab to use, the default is S:cRonTab.

TEMPLATE
 CRONTAB/K :

EXAMPLE
 CRONTAB=Zeus:StartUp/cRonTab


The logfile to write to.

TEMPLATE
 LOGFILE/K :

EXAMPLE
 LOGS:cRon.log


The default stack to use for events launched.
Value must be greater than 2084 bytes.
If no specified, the value cRon was started with
is taken.

TEMPLATE
 STACK/K/N :


The default priority to launch events with.

TEMPLATE
 PRI/K/N


The priority to run cRon with.

TEMPLATE
 CRONPRI/K/N


The name of the arexx port to use, if not given
cRon defaults to 'cRon'.

TEMPLATE
 PORTNAME/K: 


How to create cRonTab's:
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Lines in this file must be blank, a comment, or an event.  Comments are
denoted by lines that start with a "#" symbol.  Events take the form of

	min hour day month dow command <command's args, if any>

in their simplest form.  Each of min, hour, day, month and dow (day of the
week) are specifications for what range of values this command is to be run
at.  A * indicates any value is acceptable.  Numeric digits specify
specific values and can be seperated by a , (seperates distinct entries) or
a - (used to indicate a range of entries).  For example,

	* * * * * Date

would run the command date every minute of every hour of every day of every
month regardless of the day of the week.

	0 * * * * Date

is similar, but only runs the date command on the zeroth minute of each
hour.

	1,5-10,25 * * * * Date

would run the date command on minutes 1, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10 and 25 of each
hour.

Months range from 1 (January) to 12 (December).  The day of the week ranges
from 0 (Sunday) to 6 (Saturday).

There are special event option which can be used:

Event Options:
~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Give a name to an event.

TEMPLATE
	:NAME/K

EXAMPLE
	:Name WakeMeUp


After the event has been started, remove it from the event list.

TEMPLATE
	:EXECONCE/S

EXAMPLE
	:ExecOnce


If you specified a the following option then every time an event is
started or ends a message gets sent to the log file.  This turns off
logging for the specific event.  Handy for things one runs many, many
times, in keeping the size of your logfile from exploding.

TEMPLATE
	:NOLOG/S

EXAMPLE
	:NoLog


Start this command using ARexx rather than trying to run it as a system
call.  If the first character of the command is "`" then it will be
started as an ARexx string rather than a command.

TEMPLATE
	:REXX/S

EXAMPLE
	:Rexx


The stacksize to use when launching the event.

This option is ignored for ARexx events.

If the value specified is less than 2048, or this option is omitted, then
the default value will be used instead.

TEMPLATE
	:STACK/K/N

EXAMPLE
	:Stack 50000


The priority to launch the event at.
This option is ignored for ARexx events.

TEMPLATE
	:PRI/K/N

EXAMPLE
	:PRI -5


Quick setup description for use with Zeus BBS:
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
cRon resides in Zeus:Bin/3rdParty/, and cRonTab in my Zeus:StartUp/
directory.

I launch cRon from Zeus:Prefs/Progs with:

Zeus:Bin/3rdParty/cRon CRONTAB Zeus:StartUp/cRonTab \
 LOGFILE Zeus:Logs/cRon.log


The only thing you need now is to create/edit a 'cRonTab' file,
this file holds all the time and date and commands to run.

Just look at the example (the original CyberCron example)
and edit it to suit your needs.

Or just use this small one I use:

------ cut ------
# AHWBBS cRonTab for Zeus BBS Pro (04.02.96)

00 2 * * *		ZEUS:StartUp/BackUp
30 2 * * *		ZEUS:StartUp/UpdateStats
00 3 * * *		ZEUS:Rexx/Mailer/ACall.rexx 3 2:285/32
45 3 * * *		ZEUS:Rexx/Mailer/ACall.rexx 2 14:100/100
00 4 * * 0,2,4	ZEUS:Rexx/Mailer/ACall.rexx 1 21:103/1
#10 8 * * *	ZEUS:Rexx/Mailer/ACall.rexx 1 85:1/1
00 21 * * *	ZEUS:Rexx/Mailer/ACall.rexx 3 2:285/32
------ cut ------



